Source: paperman
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Simon Glass <sjg@chromium.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), qmake6, qt6-base-dev, qt6-base-dev-tools, qt6-scxml-dev, qt6-svg-dev, libpoppler-qt6-dev, libpodofo-dev, libtiff-dev, libjpeg-dev, zlib1g-dev, libsane-dev, imagemagick, tesseract-ocr, tesseract-ocr-eng
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/sjg20/paperman

Package: paperman
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, qt6-qpa-plugins, libqt6sql6-sqlite
Recommends: tesseract-ocr, qt6-gtk-platformtheme
Description: Electronic filing cabinet: scan, print, stack, arrange
 Paperman allows you to:
   - Quickly scan and file paper into your computer
   - Read and write PaperPort .max files
   - Stack, arrange and name your scanned paper
   - Easily print and view your scanned paper or convert to / from PDF
   - Paperman uses SANE and supports JPEG compression on modern, high-speed
     scanners
